UID:6a6f88b484035f0424276819@squarespace.com
DESCRIPTION:Transform Your Memories into Meaningful Narrative\nA Writing R
 etreat in Beautiful West County\nReady to tell your story? Your memories a
 re waiting to become literature.\nDiscover the power of your personal stor
 y and learn to craft it with authenticity\, depth\, and literary grace.\nW
 orkshop Overview\nJoin us for an immersive memoir writing experience desig
 ned to help you uncover\, shape\, and share the stories that have defined 
 your life. Whether you're a complete beginner or have been writing for yea
 rs\, this workshop will provide you with the tools and confidence to trans
 form your memories into compelling prose.\nWhat You will Learn:\nMemory Mi
 ning Techniques\n: Discover how to access and explore your most meaningful
  experiences\nNarrative Structure\n: Master the art of organizing your lif
 e events into engaging storylines\nVoice & Perspective\n: Develop your uni
 que authorial voice and choose the right point of view\nScene Construction
 \n: Learn to craft vivid\, cinematic scenes that bring your memories to li
 fe\nTruth vs. Accuracy\n: Navigate the ethical and creative considerations
  of memoir writing\nCharacter Development\n: Portray yourself and others w
 ith complexity and compassion\nRevision Strategies\n: Polish your work thr
 ough effective editing techniques\nWorkshop fee is $147\, $127 for OCA mem
 bers. This workshop is limited to 8 participants and will be held in the O
 CA Studio.\nRegister\nWorkshop Format\nDuration\n: One Saturday ( 4 hours 
 total).\nClass Size\n: Limited to 8 participants for personalized attentio
 n\nFormat\n: Interactive sessions combining instruction\, writing exercise
 s\, and peer feedback\nMaterials Provided\n: Writing prompts\, handouts\, 
 and recommended reading list\nWho Should Attend\nAspiring memoir writers a
 t any experience level\nAnyone interested in preserving family history\nWr
 iters looking to explore personal narrative\nIndividuals seeking therapeut
 ic writing experiences\nThose curious about the memoir genre\nWhat to Brin
 g\nNotebook and writing materials\nOpen mind and willingness to share (in 
 a supportive environment)\nNo previous writing experience necessary\nLed B
 y\nAlaura O’Dell MFA\, an experienced memoir author and writing instruct
 or\, will guide you through each step of the creative process with warmth\
 , expertise\, and encouragement. Alaura has guest lectured at Santa Rosa J
 unior College\, Marin College and Sonoma State University. O’Dell is cur
 rently working on a memoir\, which has attracted an international publishe
 r. For over 30 years she has lead women’s workshops and classes\, includ
 ing with her company\, Sacred Journeys for Women\, facilitating retreats t
 o sacred sites around the world.
LOCATION:Occidental Center for the Arts\, 3850 Doris Murphy Court\, Occide
 ntal\, CA 95465
URL:https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/memoir-writ
 ing-workshop-for-women-crafting-your-life-story
X-SOURCE:Occidental Center for the Arts, Creative Sonoma, North Bay Bohemian, Visit Santa Rosa
END:VEVENT
