BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.hannawinery.com/events/festa-dautunno/", "Press Democrat": "https://www.hannawinery.com/events/festa-dautunno/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.hannawinery.com/events/festa-dautunno/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Festa d’Autunno – “Autumn Festival”
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T170000
UID:260813W0IlB-5jaU2Zaj2cLncadQ
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the arrival of fall with an unforgettable afternoon 
 of Italian-inspired wine\, artisanal cuisine\, and sweeping vineyard views
  at HANNA Winery’s picturesque Alexander Valley Ranch.\n\nBe among the f
 irst to taste HANNA’s newest Italian varietal releases\, including Calif
 ornia’s first Grillo\, a vibrant\, citrus-driven white wine with a rich\
 , textured finish. Experience our newly released 2024 Dry Creek Mountain S
 angiovese\, a beautifully expressive interpretation of Tuscany’s iconic 
 grape. Leading up to an exclusive barrel tasting of Festeggiamo\, our new 
 Sangiovese and Nero d’Avola blend\, before its official winter release.\
 n\nEach wine will be expertly paired with authentic Italian cuisine prepar
 ed by Chef Pete Budimirovic of Casa Nostra Norcal Catering\, known for cr
 afting exceptional dishes with locally sourced organic ingredients and pre
 mium flour imported from Italy.\n\n**Pairings:**\n\n2024 HANNA Sonoma Coun
 ty Rosé with Heirloom Tomato Bruschetta\n\n2025 HANNA Dry Creek Mountain 
 Grillo *(California’s first Grillo)* with Sicilian Tuna Crudo finished
  with HANNA Estate Extra Virgin Olive Oil\n\n2024 HANNA Dry Creek Mountain
  Sangiovese with Wood Fired Margherita Pizza topped with Balsamic Glaze\n\
 nExclusive Barrel Tasting: 2025 HANNA Dry Creek Mountain Festeggiamo paire
 d with Wood Fired October Fest Pizza with Andouille Sausage\, Pickled Cher
 ry Peppers\, and Caramelized Onions.\n\n2023 HANNA Reserve Alexander Valle
 y Nero d’Avola with Crispy Arancini\n\nSweet Finale: Mini Cannoli\n\nWhe
 ther you’re passionate about Italian wines\, curious to taste California
 ’s first Grillo\, or simply looking for a memorable afternoon in Wine Co
 untry\, Festa d’Autunno promises exceptional wines\, incredible food pai
 rings\, and warm HANNA hospitality.\n\nSpace is limited—reserve your exp
 erience today and celebrate the flavors of the harvest season with us.\n\n
 **Tickets:**\n\nMembers: $55.00 per person\n\n*(up to 4 tickets per member
 ship)*\n\nGeneral Admission: $70 per person\n\nGroups of 6+ Tickets: $50 p
 er person (Code: GROUP)
LOCATION:Hanna Winery- Alexander Valley
URL:https://www.hannawinery.com/events/festa-dautunno/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sullivanwine.com/harvest-party/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Sullivan Rutherford Estate's Annual Event of Artistry & Excellence
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T180000
UID:260812OtRljeQh3kGYNJII_L_BYA
DESCRIPTION:Join us on Saturday\, September 26th from 3:00 p.m. to 6:00 p.
 m. for an afternoon celebrating excellence\, creativity\, and authenticity
  at the intersection of wine\, art\, and hospitality at Sullivan Rutherfor
 d Estate.\n\nSet against the backdrop of harvest in Rutherford\, Napa Vall
 ey\, guests will gather around a grand table for a thoughtfully curated ex
 perience featuring exceptional wines from Sullivan Rutherford Estate Winem
 aker Jeff Cole\, extraordinarily inventive cuisine from one of the Napa Va
 lley’s most renowned chefs and meaningful conversation. James Beard Awar
 d-winning Chef Rogelio Garcia will present a four-course culinary journey 
 inspired by the season's finest ingredients\, thoughtfully crafted in dial
 ogue with the artistic expressions of both ceramicist Adán Paredes and Wi
 nemaker Jeff Cole. Live music will provide the soundtrack to an afternoon 
 designed to foster connection\, celebrate creativity and a shared apprecia
 tion for craftsmanship\, artistry\, and excellence.\n\nThroughout the even
 t\, guests will have the opportunity to engage with world-renowned ceramic
  artist Adán Paredes\, whose work reflects a lifelong dedication to craft
 smanship and creative expression. Joining him will be Sullivan Rutherford 
 Estate’s Winemaker Jeff Cole\, whose own artistry takes shape in the vin
 eyard and cellar in order to produce the most iconic Merlot and Cabernet S
 auvignon expressions of Rutherford. Throughout the afternoon\, guests will
  enjoy a curated selection of wines\, including a limited preview of an un
 released bottling of our Family Reserve available exclusively for this cel
 ebration.\n\nHarvest is a season that reminds us that the most meaningful 
 experiences are rarely created alone. They emerge through patience\, colla
 boration\, dedication\, perseverance and a shared commitment to excellence
 . This celebration brings together three distinct forms of artistry: winem
 aking\, creative cuisine\, and one-of-a-kind visual expressions for an unf
 orgettable afternoon among friends. Tickets are $425 per guest\, or $550 f
 or two tickets for Founder’s Members.
LOCATION:Sullivan Rutherford Estate
URL:https://sullivanwine.com/harvest-party/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
