 ions and bibliographies\, and offers note-taking\, outlining\, and paper-w
 riting features\, including the capability to create papers via GoogleDocs
 .<br />Workshop Details: Extra Credit available!<br />This NoodleTools wor
 kshop will focus on the MLA APA citation styles.<br />Check with your inst
 ructor to confirm the citation style appropriate for your research assignm
 ent.<br />When writing a research paper\, the discipline typically determi
 nes the citation style you will use.<br />In this workshop\, you will lear
 n how to sign up for an account with NoodleTools. We will also provide exa
 mples to show how to create citations\, create a bibliography and check fo
 r errors. There will be time to ask questions at the end of the overview 
 —bring your sources along. Join us and learn how to cite your sources ri
 ght!<br />Extra Credit: As students\, you have the option to submit your i
 nstructor and course name when you register if you would like us to notify
  your instructor that you have attended the workshop for extra credit. Or\
 , you can work with your instructor on an alternative way to provide evide
 nce of your attendance.<br />Registration: (click "Begin Registration" but
 ton below)<br />This workshop requires registration in order to be admitte
 d to the Zoom meeting.<br />You will receive a confirmation email with the
  Zoom URL link for this workshop. Check your spam folder if you do not see
  it.<br />This Zoom workshop will open 10 minutes early to allow you time 
 to log on.<br />Attendees are asked to abide by SRJC student conduct polic
 y.<br />Not familiar with Zoom? Watch this 1-minute video on how to join a
  Zoom meeting.<br />Have questions? Chat with an SRJC Librarian!
