SUMMARY:Observational Drawing (6 week series) (Copy) — Sebastopol Center
  For the Arts\, California
DTSTART:20260930T000000
DTEND:20261001T000000
UID:db45bd41514fa020048c72635f589cc3@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Sale\n      \n\n\n\n\n\nObservational Drawing (6 week series) 
 (Late Add Discount Available)\n\n\n          Sale Price:\n        \n      
   $225.00 \n        \n          Original Price:\n        \n\n          $32
 5.00\n        \n\nWednesday Evenings\, 6:00-9:00pmSeptember 16th\, 23rd\, 
 30th\, October 7th\, 14th\, and 21st  $300.00 + $25.00 Materials Fee NOW 
 $200 + $25 Materials Fee Age Requirements: 18+ In this six week course\, s
 tudents will learn and practice observational skills and fundamental drawi
 ng techniques that will inform all of their other creative pursuits. This
  course is for anyone who wants to practice and advance their drawing skil
 ls - beginners\, those who haven’t practiced in years\, or any artists w
 ho just want to learn new techniques and practice their skills with consis
 tent feedback and guidance. Learning to draw is truly learning to see - a 
 skill that anyone can be taught\, practice\, and hone. Through demonstrati
 on\, practice\, and reflective discussion\, this class will explore the fo
 undations of classical drawing techniques in a low pressure environment. 
 Observational drawing gives all artists a foundation of practical knowledg
 e and skills that infinitely expands the possibilities of what one can cre
 ate. If your ideas feel limited by your drawing skills\, if you feel frust
 rated or stuck in your painting practice\, or if you simply want to start 
 drawing and are looking for a place to start\, this is the class for you.A
 bout the Instructor: Hannah Day received her BA in Visual Arts with an emp
 hasis on drawing and printmaking from University of San Diego\, then atten
 ded University of Hawaii at Manoa to receive her MFA in printmaking. Hanna
 h’s etchings have been internationally shown and collected\, but her art
  practice also includes paper cutting\, graphite\, and watercolor. She has
  taught all ages in many mediums. These days\, Hannah primarily teaches wa
 tercolor\, observational drawing\, and paper cutting. You can view her wor
 k at www.hannahdrawstrees.com  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\
 n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n          \n            \n              \n       
          Add to cart
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts\, 282 S High St\, Sebastopol\, CA 
 95472
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/observational-drawing-6-week-
 series-ng9bk
