DESCRIPTION:J. Roddy Walston is a force of nature. If his hits like Heavy 
 Bells is are a war cry\, then the deep cuts like Boys Can Never Tell are a
  tac@cal cosmic retreat. For some\, his music is a form of religion\, psyc
 hedelic in its intensity\, transforma@ve in its grip on the body\, shaking
  loose something primal that’s been buried too long. It’s not about th
 inking\, It’s about moving\, feeling\, surrendering. His influences are 
 a riot of contradic@ons: Kurt Cobain’s fury\, Nilsson’s fractured swee
 tness\, Zeppel
LOCATION:Little Saint\, 25 North Street\, Healdsburg\, California 95448\, 
