SUMMARY:Caring at the End of Life: Understanding Hospice & Palliative Care
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261001T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261001T193000
UID:260911L7j74fjLG0GYdc5ReEK1Cg
DESCRIPTION:What does it really mean to care for someone facing serious il
 lness or nearing the end of life?\n\nJoin us for October’s Death Positiv
 e Event with local specialists Cat and Lisa for a thoughtful\, practical c
 onversation about the care and support available to individuals and famili
 es navigating serious illness\, dying\, and end of life.\n\nWe’ll explor
 e:\n\n🍃 The difference between hospice and palliative care 🍃 When ea
 ch type of care may be appropriate 🍃 What hospice care really looks lik
 e 🍃 How hospice supports both patients and families 🍃 The meaningful
  role of hospice volunteers 🍃 How presence and companionship can make a
  difference at the end of life\n\nWhether you’re caring for someone now\
 , wondering what these services actually provide\, interested in volunteer
 ing\, or simply want to be better informed before the need arises\, this e
 vening offers an opportunity to learn\, ask questions\, and better underst
 and the choices and support available.\n\nOpen to all & admission is FREE!
LOCATION:Napa Valley Unitarian Universalists (NVUU)
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/1999002056964
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
