 he goal is that it prepares students to understand who they are\, build ri
 ght relationships\, examine power\, and take meaningful action with the ca
 mpus and South County community. Grounded in SRJC Petaluma's small-campus 
 experience and commitment to connection\, the framework recognizes that le
 adership develops through identity\, place\, reflection\, relationship\, a
 nd shared responsibility.  Keynote: Dr. Bryon ReavesFor more information\,
  visit the Identity and Leadership Summit website here.  &#160\;  SRJC Pet
 aluma - 680 Sonoma Mountain Pkwy\, Petaluma\, CA 94954
