DESCRIPTION:<p>Bring Your Own Binoculars and Chair! This is a guided tour 
 into the wonders of the night sky that are visible through common binocula
 rs. Guests will station their chairs in the parking lot outside the observ
 atory and knowledgeable docents with laser pointers will guide guests to t
 he hidden secrets of the night sky. Expect to see double stars\, open star
  clusters\, globular clusters\, maybe even a planet or two!<br><br>Please 
 visit <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://rfo.simpletix.com&amp\
 ;sa=D&amp\;source=calendar&amp\;ust=1759171003342407&amp\;usg=AOvVaw3EyfQ9
 iFOS_Kcc4QmBpsoM" target="_blank">https://rfo.simpletix.com</a> for import
 ant information and to buy tickets. You MUST have a ticket to attend this 
 event\; tickets will not be sold at the door. <strong>Please note that ti
 ckets are non-refundable and cannot be used for future events. </strong><
 /p><p>Cost is $35 per adult ($30 for seniors or under 18) and includes the
  State Park parking fee.</p><p> </p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20250924T184404Z
LOCATION:Robert Ferguson Observatory\, 2605 Adobe Canyon Rd\, Kenwood\, CA
  95452\, USA
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:Robert Ferguson Observatory
END:VEVENT
