X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://giving4life.org/2026-grand-bazaar/", "Press Democrat": "https://giving4life.org/2026-grand-bazaar/", "Visit Santa Rosa": "https://www.visitsantarosa.com/events/grand-bazaar-of-petaluma/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://giving4life.org/2026-grand-bazaar/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Grand Bazaar of Petaluma
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T150000
UID:260912ho1QDcXTPESFiOOqRkIwhg
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an lively\, in-person marketplace bursting with un
 ique finds from over 125 talented artists\, crafters\, and vendors\, showc
 asing a exciting mix of creative treasures — from festive holiday décor
  and gifts to rare collectibles and one-of-a-kind art. Every day brings so
 mething new to explore!\n\nBrowse an incredible selection of products\, in
 cluding jewelry\, clothing\, art\, woodworking\, glasswork\, pottery\, kid
 s’ toys\, miniatures\, candles\, soaps\, and much more. Discover beautif
 ul vintage and handmade pieces\, plus practical essentials like pet access
 ories and gift cards.  Featuring tasty treats from Sax's Joint\, Kona Ice
 \, Pupusas la Bendicion\, and more.\n\nProceeds from this event benefit Mi
 cah’s Hugs\, an inspiring local nonprofit dedicated to educating youth a
 bout the dangers of substance abuse and fentanyl poisoning.\n\nOur 2025 Gr
 and Bazaar welcomed more than 3\,000 community members and raised over $20
 \,000 to support this life-saving mission. Join us this year for an even b
 igger\, better\, and more spacious event. Together\, we can make a meaning
 ful difference for our youth—and you may even learn how to save a life.
LOCATION:Petaluma Fairgrounds
URL:https://giving4life.org/2026-grand-bazaar/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat, Visit Santa Rosa
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.thefloathousepetaluma.org/turn-to-the-river"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:"Paddle The Petaluma: Turn to The River" Guided Kayak Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T120000
UID:260514Bg594FnxW0a5CHLFtcYKcg
DESCRIPTION:Paddle the Petaluma: Turn to The River is a relaxed\, beginner
 -friendly guided kayak tour exploring the past\, present\, and future of P
 etaluma’s historic waterway. Launching right from downtown at The Floath
 ouse Petaluma\, you'll take part in this Sonoma County Signature Experienc
 e by spending about 90 minutes on the water in stable sit-on-top kayaks\, 
 traveling a gentle mile-and-a-half route through “Petaluma’s Longest P
 ark.”\n\nAlong the way\, you’ll raft up at docks around town\, fascina
 ting  landmarks\, and riverfront gathering spaces to hear stories about h
 ow this Gold Rush-era “saltwater highway” helped shape Petaluma—and 
 how today’s community is continuing to reinvent and reconnect with the r
 iver. This isn’t just a history tour. You’ll also learn about the peop
 le\, businesses\, artists\, nonprofits\, and river advocates helping shape
  the waterway’s future right now.\n\nEverything is included in the $75 e
 xperience: kayak\, gear\, knowledgeable local guides\, insider river stori
 es\, and post-paddle perks at nearby businesses. Finish with plenty of tim
 e for brunch\, coffee\, shopping\, or simply hanging out downtown by the w
 ater. No experience necessary.\n\nNote: The Floathouse Petaluma is a nonpr
 ofit project dedicated to “putting butts in boats and smiles on faces”
  by offering year-round easy access to the Petaluma River in and on people
 -powered water craft through rentals\, events\, classes\, lessons and summ
 er camps.
LOCATION:The Floathouse Petaluma
URL:https://www.thefloathousepetaluma.org/turn-to-the-river
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
