X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Napa Valley Museum Yountville FREE Oct 3-4 Bank of America Museums
  on Us
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T160000
UID:260925C-udt7unfUO7t9voyTNb5Q
DESCRIPTION:Bank of America cardholders receive free general admission to 
 participating museums nationwide on the first full weekend of each month\;
  this month is October 3-4. \n\nAs a chill settles in the air\, Halloween
  costumes are planned\, and leaves crunch on the ground\, take a moment th
 is busy fall season to enjoy a very special exhibit in your own backyard! 
 The Napa Valley Museum Yountville has exciting exhibits including Mary Bla
 ir: Mid-Century Magic\, a special exhibition by the Walt Disney Family Mus
 eum exploring the creative vision and achievements of one of Walt Disney
 ’s most imaginative and renowned designers and art directors. Mary’s w
 ork appeared in classic Disney animated films like Cinderella (1950)\, Ali
 ce in Wonderland (1951)\, and Peter Pan (1953). The exhibit closes October
  25\, 2026\, so it might be your last chance to make it before it’s gone
 !\n\nBank of America Museums on Us program offers FREE weekend general adm
 ission on the first full weekend of every month to Bank of America\, Merri
 ll and Bank of America Private Bank credit and debit cardholders. All you 
 need is your Bank of America\, Merrill\, or Bank of America Private Bank c
 ard and picture ID for access. \n\nAdditional participating museums can b
 e found here: https://about.bankofamerica.com/en/making-an-impact/museums-
 on-us-partner
LOCATION:Napa Valley Museum Yountville
URL:https://about.bankofamerica.com/en/making-an-impact/museums-on-us-part
 ners
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://jacklondonpark.com/dia-de-muertos-2026/", "Press Democrat": "https://jacklondonpark.com/dia-de-muertos-2026/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://jacklondonpark.com/dia-de-muertos-2026/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Dia de Muertos at Jack London State Historic Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T170000
UID:260921Sd3TE50Rc0G_tNaYRNOI2Q
DESCRIPTION:In recognition of Día de Muertos\, Jack London State Historic
  Park will present two ofrendas in the House of Happy Walls Museum from Oc
 t. 4 to Nov. 6\, 2026.\n\nDia de Muertos\, or Day of the Dead\, is a tradi
 tion that began in Mexican and other Latino cultures.  An ofrenda\, Spani
 sh for ‘offering\,’ is an altar created to honor and welcome the memor
 y of those who have died.\n\nThe Legacy Ofrenda will honor writer and adve
 nturer Jack London\, Charmian London\, and other individuals connected to 
 the history of the property. Through photographs\, reproductions\, traditi
 onal elements of an ofrenda\, and carefully selected symbolic objects\, th
 e installation will reflect Jack and Charmian's partnership\, writing and 
 travels\, their life at Beauty Ranch\, their connection to the land\, and 
 the legacies they left behind.\n\nThe Community Ofrenda will be a shared\,
  participatory offering. Visitors\, locals\, volunteers\, Board members\, 
 and employees can contribute a small photograph\, written name\, memory\, 
 drawing or message honoring someone who has passed away – including a be
 loved pet. \n\nThe installation will grow throughout October as more peop
 le participate.  Materials will be available at the display for visitors 
 who would like to join the celebration and contribute a name\, memory or e
 ven a drawing of their loved one.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/dia-de-muertos-2026/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://kickwheelsonoma.com/products/clay-and-bloom-workshop-with-deanna-and-gena-sunday-october-4th", "Press Democrat": "https://kickwheelsonoma.com/products/clay-and-bloom-workshop-with-deanna-and-gena-sunday-october-4th"}
