BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://cmvineyard.com/visit/", "Press Democrat": "https://cmvineyard.com/visit/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://cmvineyard.com/visit/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:A Taste of Italy at Centennial Mountain Tasting Room
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T170000
UID:260430JmHtQ2Mft0WZzBOoc1-3Zw
DESCRIPTION:For wine drinkers eager to experience world-class wines made i
 n California from Italian varieties\, the Centennial Mountain Tasting Room
  is a must during any trip to Sonoma County. Located just off the plaza in
  the charming town of Healdsburg near famed restaurants\, boutiques and ga
 lleries\, the Centennial Mountain Tasting Room is a destination that invit
 es discovery. Founded by the acclaimed team that guides renowned Pinot Noi
 r and Chardonnay producer Rhys Vineyards\, Centennial Mountain was establi
 shed to explore Italian grape varieties grown on its acclaimed Centennial 
 Mountain Vineyard in the rugged mountains of Northern Sonoma County.\n\nTh
 e Centennial Mountain Vineyard Tasting features the winery’s coveted Neb
 biolo\, and the pioneering Carricante and Nerello Mascalese wines\, among 
 others. To showcase how beautifully the wines pair with food\, the winery 
 also offers a delicious Wine and Sushi Pairing from nearby Asahi Sushi\, o
 ne of Healdsburg’s most popular dining destinations.\n\nGuests can also 
 enhance their tasting experience with a curated salumi board from Journeym
 an Meat Company. This generous accompaniment features six house-made salum
 i\, crostini\, cornichons\, olives\, and a selection of local cheese that 
 serves 2 to 5 guests.
LOCATION:Centennial Mountain Tasting Room 
URL:https://cmvineyard.com/visit/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://about.bankofamerica.com/en/making-an-impact/museums-on-us-partners"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Sonoma Valley Museum of Art FREE October 3-4 Bank of America Museu
 ms on Us
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T170000
UID:260925V8W4rP9DNUOdXLr4ox5Qeg
DESCRIPTION:Bank of America cardholders receive free general admission to 
 participating museums nationwide on the first full weekend of each month\;
  this month is October 3-4. \n\nAs a chill settles in the air\, Halloween
  costumes are planned\, and leaves crunch on the ground\, take a moment th
 is busy fall season to enjoy local culture! The Sonoma Valley Museum of Ar
 t has exciting exhibits including brand new installation The Real-Life Art
  History of M. Louise Stanley\, an exhibit sponsored by Bank of America th
 at celebrates a unique Bay Area Figurative artist for her wildly imaginati
 ve narratives and distinctly female perspective\, shaped by her keen obser
 vations of everyday life and setting her apart from her male contemporarie
 s. The exhibit features Sanley’s large-scale acrylic paintings\, gouache
  and watercolor works on paper\, sculptural objects\, sketchbooks\, studie
 s\, photos\, and notes from her personal archives\, showing the artist’s
  perspective across multiple media forms. \n\nBank of America Museums on 
 Us program offers FREE weekend general admission on the first full weekend
  of every month to Bank of America\, Merrill and Bank of America Private B
 ank credit and debit cardholders. All you need is your Bank of America\, M
 errill\, or Bank of America Private Bank card and picture ID for access. 
 \n\nAdditional participating museums can be found here: https://about.bank
 ofamerica.com/en/making-an-impact/museums-on-us-partner
LOCATION:Sonoma Valley Museum of Art
URL:https://about.bankofamerica.com/en/making-an-impact/museums-on-us-part
 ners
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
