SUMMARY:The Madrona Debuts Garden Supper Club in Healdsburg
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T193000
UID:260915iI5b6ZwGTUmPoz65Iak_6g
DESCRIPTION:On Thursday\, October 8 at 6pm\, The Madrona\, the two-MICHELI
 N Key boutique hotel and restaurant in Healdsburg\, will debut the inaugur
 al Madrona Garden Supper Club\, a new dining series celebrating the beauty
 \, abundance and changing seasons of the historic estate’s garden.\n\nDe
 signed as an intimate dinner party of just 30 guests\, The Madrona Garden 
 Supper Club offers a firsthand look at the property’s onsite regenerativ
 e gardens and how they drive the culinary program and seasonal menus. The 
 experience begins in the Citrus Grove with welcome cocktails \\(or spirit-
 free alternatives\\) and seasonal canapés\, followed by a chef-guided wal
 k through The Madrona’s garden to explore the harvested ingredients insp
 iring the night’s menu. Guests will then sit down along Garden Lane for 
 a four-course dinner \\(and optional wine pairing\\) inspired entirely by 
 what is growing in the garden at that very moment.\n\nWhat: The Madrona Ga
 rden Supper Club: Autumn\n\nWhen: Thursday\, October 8 at 6pm\n\nWhere: Th
 e Madrona\, 1001 Westside Road\, Healdsburg\n\nPrice: $150 per person with
  optional wine or non-alcoholic pairing \\($65 per person\\)\n\nRSVP: Seat
 s are limited\, so RSVPs through OpenTable are required.\n\nThe Madrona Ga
 rden Supper Club will continue to evolve with the seasons\, with new dates
  in 2027 to be announced and each menu curated around what’s freshest in
  the garden.
LOCATION:The Madrona
URL:https://www.opentable.com/booking/experiences-availability?rid=8088&re
 stref=8088&experienceId=791873&utm_source=external&utm_medium=referral&utm
 _campaign=shared
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.bandsintown.com/e/1039265372?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=287&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Shannon Lay & Calvin Love
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T000000
UID:260813K0yOpXO4ckqHBu0Zb_zVqg
DESCRIPTION:Shannon Lay’s music is shored by radical empathy. After 15 y
 ears of writing\, recording and performing her singularly gentle songs in 
 venues around the world\, the self-taught singer-songwriter is most concer
 ned with how her music may help people in emotional and spiritual need. In
  a world of persistent change\, Lay’s goal is to have concentrations of 
 love and energy in her work that double as a helping hand or a voice whisp
 ering “everything is going to be ok.” The singer’s abiding belief is
  that immense change also means invaluable transformation and permanent re
 lief. Intention is her North Star. Hailed by publications such as Pitchfor
 k\, The Guardian\, SPIN and Uncut magazine\, Lay’s solo albums\, includi
 ng “Geist\,” “August”\, “Living Water\,” and “All this life 
 goin’ down” are noted for their thoughtful and entirely tender reflect
 ions on life’s big questions. Her seraphic voice has drawn comparisons t
 o British folk icons Anne Briggs\, Sandy Denny and Vashti Bunyan. Though a
 n old soul\, Lay aims to meet her listeners in the present. For her\, crea
 ting a song\, a recording or a live performance that is relatable and comm
 unal is of the utmost importance for we are constantly in flux and those u
 nknowns\, met with compassion\, can be beautiful. \n\nWritten by Erin Osm
 on
LOCATION:Little Saint
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/1039265372?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=2
 87&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
