SUMMARY:Retos en las Montañas (Challenges in the Mountains)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T150000
UID:260917yGuCqegEqUKeKUb_WAGNXg
DESCRIPTION:Join Jack London Park Partners and Sonoma Ecology Center staff
  in a series of intermediate hikes\, guided in Spanish\, between Jack Lond
 on State Historic Park and Sugarloaf Ridge State Park. Each hike is a roun
 d trip\, returning to the starting point\, and will increase in length or 
 difficulty. Not appropriate for children under 12 years old.\n\n1.    
  Sat. Oct. 10 – Jack London's Ancient Redwood. 3.72 miles\, 620 ft. elev
 ation \\(meet at Jack London State Historic Park\\).\n\n2.     Sat. Oc
 t. 17 – Sugarloaf's waterfall loop. 2.39 miles\, 610 ft. elevation \\(me
 et at Sugarloaf Ridge State Park\\).\n\n3.     Sat. Oct. 24 – Upper 
 Fallen to Camp Via to Fern Lake at Jack London. 5.72 miles\, 1\,150 ft. el
 evation \\(meet at Jack London State Historic Park\\).\n\n4.     Sat. 
 Nov. 7 – Gunsight Rock at Sugarloaf/Hood Mountain Regional Park. 6.44 mi
 les\, 2\,129 ft. elevation \\(meet at Sugarloaf Ridge State Park\\).\n\n5.
      Sun. Nov. 15 – Sonoma Ridge in Sonoma Developmental Center/Jack
  London. 9.67 miles\, 2\,126 ft. elevation \\(meet at the intersection of 
 Arnold Dr. and Harney Rd.\, inside the SDC\\).\n\n6.     Sat.  Nov. 2
 1 – "The Big Loop" at Sugarloaf. 7.37 miles\, 1\,739 ft elevation \\(mee
 t at Sugarloaf Ridge State Park\\).
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/reto2026
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
