SUMMARY:2026 Children's Jamboree & Marketplace
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T140000
UID:260906Usl7XRIE0kuQtQjGybulSA
DESCRIPTION:2026 Children's Jamboree & Marketplace - Come Grow\, Learn\, P
 lay\, and Shop with Us!\n\nThis fun\, free event for children and adults i
 s Sunday\, October 11 from 11 a.m. to 2 p.m. at Nokhnoma Teaching and Demo
 nstration Garden in Santa Rosa.\n\nActivities for children will include it
 ems they can make and take home such as corn husk dolls\, sun catchers\, g
 ratitude banners\, seed pots\, garden art rocks\, and more! ﻿ ﻿\n\nMar
 ketplace will feature an assortment of 4-inch and 1-gallon succulents\, su
 cculent containers\, succulent topped pumpkins in assorted sizes\, small a
 nd medium wreaths crafted with flora\, cones and/or succulents\, oyster sh
 ell succulents and decoupage oyster shell ornaments\, beaded light catcher
 s\, and gardening books. All proceeds benefit the UC Master Gardener Progr
 am of Sonoma County. Cash\, checks and credit cards accepted.\n\nInformati
 on tables will be staffed with Sonoma County Master Gardener volunteers wh
 o will share home gardening information\, answer your home gardening-relat
 ed questions and provide information about our programs and projects.\n\nP
 artner organizations on site will include the Girl Scouts\, Sonoma County 
 Bee Association\, Children's Museum of Sonoma County\, Master Food Preserv
 ers\, Zero Waste\, Sonoma County 4-H\, and others.\n\nRegister to attend: 
 Go to https://tinyurl.com/5dk8nw7r or sonomamg.ucanr.edu/ Upcoming Events
  to complete your registration. After registering\, you will receive a con
 firmation email containing information about attending the event.\n\nGener
 al information\n\nADA-compliant porta potty on site.\n\nADA parking will b
 e available.\n\nWater available for filling water bottles.\n\nWear comfort
 able\, closed-toe shoes suitable for walking on unpaved\, uneven paths\n\n
 Bring a hat if desired.\n\nNo animals allowed\, except trained service dog
 s.\n\nFood and beverages will not be available\, bring your own snacks or 
 picnic lunch.
LOCATION:Nokhnoma Teaching and Demonstration Garden
URL:https://tinyurl.com/5dk8nw7r
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
