X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Occidental Center for the Arts": "https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/david-luning-friends", "North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/david-luning-friends"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Occidental Center for the Arts": "https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/david-luning-friends"}
X-SOURCE-ID:occidental_arts
SUMMARY:John Prine Tribute with David Luning\, Jason Crosby\, Ben Dubin an
 d Victoria George
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T200000
UID:6a137d11fdf9506a76bad2f3@squarespace.com
DESCRIPTION:David Luning\, who attended Harmony School (now OCA) returns t
 o our stage for a special tribute celebrating John Prine's birthday. David
  will be joined by impressive musical colleagues Jason Crosby\, Ben Dubin 
 and Victoria George.\nTickets are $35\, $30 for OCA members.\nGet Tickets\
 nThis show will take place in our auditorium. Doors open at 5:30 PM.\nDavi
 d Luning knew at a young age the path his life should take. Throughout gen
 erations\, troubadours and singers have harnessed the cultural landscape a
 nd passed it along\, with the likes of John Prine and Townes Van Zandt pav
 ing the way with the telling of their stories. Following in those footstep
 s\, the Sonoma County singer/songwriter's new record is the product of a m
 assive turn in his life and taps into that cultural archive. Listening to 
 ‘Souvenirs’ by John Prine\, was a cornerstone moment\, compelling Luni
 ng to leave Berklee College and follow in the tradition of these iconic tr
 oubadours.\nLearn more about David Luning.
LOCATION:Occidental Center for the Arts\, 3850 Doris Murphy Court\, Occide
 ntal
URL:https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/david-lunin
 g-friends
X-SOURCE:Occidental Center for the Arts, North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
