BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://beelinerooftop.getbento.com/event/raw-rogue/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Raw & Rogue
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261013T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261013T210000
UID:260912ao_EHDrHSEKsu2N5sv5ZnQ
DESCRIPTION:For three Tuesdays this fall\, Raw \\+ Rogue brings an intimat
 e twelve-seat omakase experience to the rooftop of Appellation Healdsburg.
  Across twelve courses\, Chef Willer Larreal Perez—a Venezuela-born chef
  trained at omakase counters in Los Angeles and Miami—builds each dish a
 round the fish\, taking guests on a scenic culinary journey from the count
 er to the plate. An amuse opens the experience and dessert brings it to a 
 close\, while wine pairings from Baron Ziegler\, co-founder of Healdsburg
 ’s Banshee Wines and founder of Marine Layer\, move alongside the menu. 
 Each course is paired with its own song\, creating a soundtrack that build
 s plate by plate as the light shifts over Northern Sonoma County. Together
 \, the food\, wine and music create a multisensory evening designed to unf
 old in rhythm with the rooftop setting. \n\nWhen: Tuesdays | September 29
 \, October 13\, October 27 \\(6:30 pm\\) \n\nPrice: $295 per guest\, wine
  selections prices separately \n\nReservations are available through Open
 Table: Raw & Rogue \n\nPre-paid reservations are required.
LOCATION:Appellation Healdsburg
URL:https://beelinerooftop.getbento.com/event/raw-rogue/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.facebook.com/events/967862809218851/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Poetry Book Club: Shadow of Heaven by Ellen Bryant Voigt
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261013T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261013T190000
UID:260925qOsdpMM4g0OMCeQHAUKxTw
DESCRIPTION:Each month\, the Poetry Book Club meets online to discuss one 
 must-read book of poems\, whether a timeless classic or an award-winning c
 ontemporary. Led by Napa poet Kathleen Patterson\, who has been an enthusi
 astic book club member since its beginning\, meetings are open to all leve
 ls of poetry readers\, both the curious and the committed. ABOUT THE BOOK 
 Shortlisted for the 2002 National Book Award in Poetry. Following her stri
 ngent and much-acclaimed Kyrie\, finalist for the National Book Critics Ci
 rcle Award\, Ellen Bryant Voigt now examines more intimately the ordeals a
 nd exaltations of everyday life. Nature\, both fierce and benign\, infuses
  this collection\, furthering "an art at once ravishing and stern and deep
 ly human" \\(American Academy of Arts and Letters\\). ABOUT THE AUTHOR Ell
 en Bryant Voigt \\(1943—2025\\) was the author of eight volumes of poetr
 y\, including Messenger\, a finalist for the National Book Award and the P
 ulitzer Prize. Her numerous honors included fellowships from the Guggenhei
 m and MacArthur foundations.
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/967862809218851/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
