SUMMARY:Retos en las Montañas (Challenges in the Mountains) #2
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T150000
UID:260917IuaAaoD3-EKEXmpu5X5cjg
DESCRIPTION:Join Jack London Park Partners and Sonoma Ecology Center staff
  in a series of intermediate hikes\, guided in Spanish\, between Jack Lond
 on State Historic Park and Sugarloaf Ridge State Park. Each hike is a roun
 d trip\, returning to the starting point\, and will increase in length or 
 difficulty. Not appropriate for children under 12 years old.\n\nSat. Oct. 
 17 – Sugarloaf's waterfall loop. 2.39 miles\, 610 ft. elevation (meet at
  Sugarloaf Ridge State Park).\n\nSat. Oct. 24 – Upper Fallen to Camp Via
  to Fern Lake at Jack London. 5.72 miles\, 1\,150 ft. elevation (meet at J
 ack London State Historic Park).\n\nSat. Nov. 7 – Gunsight Rock at Sugar
 loaf/Hood Mountain Regional Park. 6.44 miles\, 2\,129 ft. elevation (meet 
 at Sugarloaf Ridge State Park).\n\nSun. Nov. 15 – Sonoma Ridge in Sonoma
  Developmental Center/Jack London. 9.67 miles\, 2\,126 ft. elevation (meet
  at the intersection of Arnold Dr. and Harney Rd.\, inside the SDC).\n\nSa
 t.  Nov. 21 – "The Big Loop" at Sugarloaf. 7.37 miles\, 1\,739 ft eleva
 tion (meet at Sugarloaf Ridge State Park).
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/reto2026
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
