X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:4th Annual NAMIWalks Sonoma County
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T130000
UID:260812WwwQzCqgT0SxsX1hBtQvXw
DESCRIPTION:Help us show that mental health is a priority.\n\nNAMI Sonoma 
 County strives to make our communities a place where everyone who  experi
 ences mental health challenges\, whether as an individual or as a family m
 ember\, friend or caregiver\, recognizes the warning signs\, can access ne
 eded  care and support\, and knows where to ask for help if needed. Help 
 us grow awareness and build a caring community. It’s free and open to al
 l!\n\nHere’s what to expect on October 17th:\n\nGet to know over 20 comm
 unity mental health organizations.\n\nEnjoy live music from the Russian Ri
 ver Ramblers.\n\nHonor a loved one or your own journey at our “Why I Wa
 lk” table. \n\nChoose to walk or just hang out and enjoy! \n\nTake yo
 ur chances on wonderful raffle prizes!\n\nEnjoy activities for kids and ki
 ds at heart.\n\nCuddle with a PALS support dog!\n\nBring your water bottle
  and your friendly\, leashed dog.\n\nFor over 40 years\, NAMI Sonoma Count
 y has provided free mental health education\, support\, awareness and advo
 cacy to our communities.  Your presence will help us to raise both fundin
 g that keeps our programs free of cost to participants and creates awarene
 ss.\n\nRegister at www.namiwalks.org/sonomacounty.\n\nSee you on OCtober 1
 7th!
LOCATION:Howarth Park - Cypress Point A picnic area
URL:https://namiwalks.org/sonomacounty
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.thefloathousepetaluma.org/turn-to-the-river"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:"Paddle The Petaluma: Turn to The River" Guided Kayak Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T120000
UID:260514xDJKp_aXUEewvinRoDEObw
DESCRIPTION:Paddle the Petaluma: Turn to The River is a relaxed\, beginner
 -friendly guided kayak tour exploring the past\, present\, and future of P
 etaluma’s historic waterway. Launching right from downtown at The Floath
 ouse Petaluma\, you'll take part in this Sonoma County Signature Experienc
 e by spending about 90 minutes on the water in stable sit-on-top kayaks\, 
 traveling a gentle mile-and-a-half route through “Petaluma’s Longest P
 ark.”\n\nAlong the way\, you’ll raft up at docks around town\, fascina
 ting  landmarks\, and riverfront gathering spaces to hear stories about h
 ow this Gold Rush-era “saltwater highway” helped shape Petaluma—and 
 how today’s community is continuing to reinvent and reconnect with the r
 iver. This isn’t just a history tour. You’ll also learn about the peop
 le\, businesses\, artists\, nonprofits\, and river advocates helping shape
  the waterway’s future right now.\n\nEverything is included in the $75 e
 xperience: kayak\, gear\, knowledgeable local guides\, insider river stori
 es\, and post-paddle perks at nearby businesses. Finish with plenty of tim
 e for brunch\, coffee\, shopping\, or simply hanging out downtown by the w
 ater. No experience necessary.\n\nNote: The Floathouse Petaluma is a nonpr
 ofit project dedicated to “putting butts in boats and smiles on faces”
  by offering year-round easy access to the Petaluma River in and on people
 -powered water craft through rentals\, events\, classes\, lessons and summ
 er camps.
LOCATION:The Floathouse Petaluma
URL:https://www.thefloathousepetaluma.org/turn-to-the-river
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
