X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:In Conversation: M. Louise Stanley and Maria Porges
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T150000
UID:260919zdIOodtLTEqPao602daMag
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an illuminating conversation between artist M. Lou
 ise Stanley and artist and writer Maria Porges as they explore works in Th
 e Real-Life Art History of M. Louise Stanley. Stanley will reflect on her 
 five-decade practice\, distinctive humor\, and playful engagement with art
  history\, mythology\, feminism\, and contemporary life. Maria Porges brin
 gs the perspective of both an accomplished artist and longtime art writer 
 whose work has appeared in Artforum\, Art in America\, the New York Times 
 Book Review\, and Hyperallergic. A recipient of SFMOMA’s SECA Award\, Po
 rges has exhibited widely and is a professor at California College of the 
 Arts. Saturday\, Oct 17\, 3 PM $25 SVMA Members | $30 non-members Pre-regi
 stration is required.
LOCATION:Sonoma Valley Museum of Art
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1419583396723164/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
