X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.thefloathousepetaluma.org/turn-to-the-river"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:"Paddle The Petaluma: Turn to The River" Guided Kayak Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T120000
UID:260514Yr3fV92sVkGrVulWgTKupA
DESCRIPTION:Paddle the Petaluma: Turn to The River is a relaxed\, beginner
 -friendly guided kayak tour exploring the past\, present\, and future of P
 etaluma’s historic waterway. Launching right from downtown at The Floath
 ouse Petaluma\, you'll take part in this Sonoma County Signature Experienc
 e by spending about 90 minutes on the water in stable sit-on-top kayaks\, 
 traveling a gentle mile-and-a-half route through “Petaluma’s Longest P
 ark.”\n\nAlong the way\, you’ll raft up at docks around town\, fascina
 ting  landmarks\, and riverfront gathering spaces to hear stories about h
 ow this Gold Rush-era “saltwater highway” helped shape Petaluma—and 
 how today’s community is continuing to reinvent and reconnect with the r
 iver. This isn’t just a history tour. You’ll also learn about the peop
 le\, businesses\, artists\, nonprofits\, and river advocates helping shape
  the waterway’s future right now.\n\nEverything is included in the $75 e
 xperience: kayak\, gear\, knowledgeable local guides\, insider river stori
 es\, and post-paddle perks at nearby businesses. Finish with plenty of tim
 e for brunch\, coffee\, shopping\, or simply hanging out downtown by the w
 ater. No experience necessary.\n\nNote: The Floathouse Petaluma is a nonpr
 ofit project dedicated to “putting butts in boats and smiles on faces”
  by offering year-round easy access to the Petaluma River in and on people
 -powered water craft through rentals\, events\, classes\, lessons and summ
 er camps.
LOCATION:The Floathouse Petaluma
URL:https://www.thefloathousepetaluma.org/turn-to-the-river
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://jacklondonpark.com/dia-de-muertos-2026/", "Press Democrat": "https://jacklondonpark.com/dia-de-muertos-2026/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://jacklondonpark.com/dia-de-muertos-2026/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Dia de Muertos at Jack London State Historic Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T170000
UID:260921FRkQEbOv3kOG9dZEmRsxCg
DESCRIPTION:In recognition of Día de Muertos\, Jack London State Historic
  Park will present two ofrendas in the House of Happy Walls Museum from Oc
 t. 4 to Nov. 6\, 2026.\n\nDia de Muertos\, or Day of the Dead\, is a tradi
 tion that began in Mexican and other Latino cultures.  An ofrenda\, Spani
 sh for ‘offering\,’ is an altar created to honor and welcome the memor
 y of those who have died.\n\nThe Legacy Ofrenda will honor writer and adve
 nturer Jack London\, Charmian London\, and other individuals connected to 
 the history of the property. Through photographs\, reproductions\, traditi
 onal elements of an ofrenda\, and carefully selected symbolic objects\, th
 e installation will reflect Jack and Charmian's partnership\, writing and 
 travels\, their life at Beauty Ranch\, their connection to the land\, and 
 the legacies they left behind.\n\nThe Community Ofrenda will be a shared\,
  participatory offering. Visitors\, locals\, volunteers\, Board members\, 
 and employees can contribute a small photograph\, written name\, memory\, 
 drawing or message honoring someone who has passed away – including a be
 loved pet. \n\nThe installation will grow throughout October as more peop
 le participate.  Materials will be available at the display for visitors 
 who would like to join the celebration and contribute a name\, memory or e
 ven a drawing of their loved one.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/dia-de-muertos-2026/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sonomabg.org/visit/maple-magic-winter-wonder/", "Press Democrat": "https://sonomabg.org/visit/maple-magic-winter-wonder/"}
