BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/reuse-in-art-reuse-in-life-a-conversation-between?aff=cityspark"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Reuse in Art\, Reuse in Life: A Conversation Between Ali Gass and 
 Phoebe Schenker
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T163000
UID:260924ngBpCzSPB0K-qIuBTveD2g
DESCRIPTION:Join Alison Gass\, Founding Executive Director of the ICA San 
 Francisco\, and Phoebe Schenker\, Executive Director of Reuse Alliance\, f
 or a wide-ranging conversation about reuse in contemporary and historical 
 art and why it is more relevant than ever.\n\nThe discussion will explore 
 the many ways artists have engaged with reuse\, from incorporating found a
 nd reclaimed materials to making reuse itself a central subject of their w
 ork. Together\, Gass and Schenker will consider how reuse connects to broa
 der cultural conversations about creativity\, sustainability\, consumption
 \, and value\, while also exploring how reuse can become a creative practi
 ce in our own everyday lives.
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/reuse-in-art-reuse-in-life
 -a-conversation-between?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108761352?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=287&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Richard Turgeon
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T160000
UID:260910sf3n1Q5ZgUO7_0xZYxNqrA
DESCRIPTION:Richard Turgeon is a San Francisco-based singer/songwriter\, m
 ulti-instrumentalist and record producer. His alternative rock sound has b
 een called "California Rock" or "New Vintage Rock\," is regularly featured
  on SiriusXM\, and has been featured in indie film soundtracks. He's curre
 ntly playing live shows in the Bay Area and beyond with his trio\, RT3.\n\
 nLast year he played drums for national act Donnie Emerson\, subject of th
 e film "Dreamin' Wild\," and Pavement co-founder Scott Kannberg recently s
 hared Rich's cover/video of Pavement's song "Date with IKEA."\n\nHis criti
 cally acclaimed solo records from the last several years have made innumer
 able “best of” lists from various press outlets\, radio stations and b
 loggers from around the world. Visit his website at www.richardturgeon.com
LOCATION:Brewsters Beer Garden
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108761352?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://eventvesta.com/events/160340/t/tickets"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Haunted Wine Tour & Tasting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T173000
UID:260831qJDuR9of_Eu5Jqo_Tk5TDQ
DESCRIPTION:This fall\, Buena Vista Winery invites you to uncover the myst
 eries\, legends\, and ghostly encounters woven into more than 165 years of
  history. Led by Sonoma historian and actor George Webber\, this immersive
  90 minute experience journeys through the historic Press House and Champa
 gne Cellars\, revealing true tales of unexplained happenings reported by B
 uena Vista team members and visitors throughout the years.\n\nHear the sto
 ries of the Glowing Ghostly Shirt\, the Little Girl Who Says Hi\, the myst
 erious Ghost Party on the Second Floor\, the Old Man Who Walked Into a Sto
 ne Wall\, and other strange occurrences that continue to add to the legend
  of Buena Vista.\n\nAlong the way\, explore some of the winery’s most in
 triguing spaces\, including the Bubble Lounge\, Cave of Curiosities\, and 
 Wine Tool Museum\, while enjoying five Buena Vista wines tasted throughout
  the experience\, including a taste drawn directly from barrel.\n\nAnd\, a
 s with any journey through Buena Vista’s extraordinary past\, you never 
 quite know when the winery’s legendary founder\, Count Agoston Haraszthy
 \, may choose to make an appearance.\n\nHistory\, wine\, mystery\, and per
 haps a spirit or two await.
LOCATION:Buena Vista Historical Winery
URL:https://eventvesta.com/events/160340/t/tickets
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.northbayoa.org/", "Press Democrat": "https://www.northbayoa.org/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.northbayoa.org/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Overeaters Anonymous (OA) Newcomer Meeting in Santa Rosa
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T170000
UID:260212Li6RI6TFNkulNV8UvONfhg
DESCRIPTION:**Is Food a Problem for You? You Are Not Alone.**\n\nOvereater
 s Anonymous (OA) is a fellowship of people who support each other in recov
 ering from compulsive eating and food behaviors. If you feel you have a pr
 oblem with food\, OA welcomes you—no matter what your background\, belie
 fs\, or eating habits.\n\nWe hold an in-person newcomer meeting on **Sunda
 ys from 4:00 – 5:00 PM** **at Christ Church United Methodist\, 1717 Yulu
 pa Ave.\, Room #4\, Santa Rosa**. Contact: Abigail (707) 293-5888. You may
  view all North Bay OA in-person and online meetings at https://www.northb
 ayoa.org/meetings.html .\n\nIn OA\, members experience **spiritual\, emoti
 onal\, and physical recovery** by practicing the **Twelve Steps** and livi
 ng by their spiritual principles—one day at a time.\n\nOA is **not** a d
 iet club or calorie-counting program.\n\nMembers have different plans of e
 ating.\n\nOA does **not** endorse any specific food plan.\n\nIf food is ca
 using problems in your life\, you don’t have to struggle alone. Recovery
  is possible\, and help is available.\n\n**Visit:** https://www.northbayoa
 .org/\n\n**Find a meeting:** https://www.northbayoa.org/meetings.html
LOCATION:Christ Church United Methodist
URL:https://www.northbayoa.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sec.regfox.com/2026-ocjourn", "Press Democrat": "https://sec.regfox.com/2026-ocjourn", "Visit Santa Rosa": "https://www.visitsantarosa.com/events/slow-meditative-birding-journey/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sec.regfox.com/2026-ocjourn"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Slow Meditative Birding Journey
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T163000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T183000
UID:260907W6ISBPe5z0efXmPJSpynyA
DESCRIPTION:Do you enjoy a slow walk in a valley\, breezes\, wil
 dflowers\, the sounds of songbirds\, the taste of a Douglas Fir
  needle or a California Bay leaf\, the aroma of Tarweed\, or w
 atching wild turkeys and California Quail hunt for seeds and ins
 ects in the grass? Join Certified California Naturalists and Suga
 rloaf docents for this series of meandering explorations. Each mo
 nth (weather permitting) we will explore one or two of our thre
 e accessible trails-- the Creekside Trail\, the Nature Trail\, an
 d the Meadow trail. Suitable for all levels and a range of mob
 ility\, these Sunday afternoon adventures will accommodate people 
 using walkers or wheelchairs\, young children\, parents with babie
 s in strollers\, as well as those who just enjoy slow walks in
  nature that stimulate the five senses. \n\nOur October outing w
 ill focus on meditative birding. We will start off by sitting q
 uietly for 10 minutes with Merlin app recording in 3 different 
 locations\, followed by about 10 minutes of discussion of the bi
 rds we heard\, using Cornell to confirm their calls and songs b
 efore moving onto the next sitting spot. We will also saunter (
 while looking for birds) between the locations for a total dista
 nce of ~1.3 miles on an accessible trail. Birding by ear lends
  itself to meditation because it works best when you sit silent
 ly and listening closely (i.e.\, if Merlin *hears* something you
  did not\, it reminds you that your mind has wandered). \n\nTic
 kets are $5 for adults and free for children under 18 years of
  age. All minors must be accompanied by parent or legal guardia
 n. **Tickets day-of\, on site will be $10 and might not be ava
 ilable.** Meet at the White Barn parking lot.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/2026-ocjourn
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat, Visit Santa Rosa
END:VEVENT
