SUMMARY:Sistah 2 Sistah
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261103T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261103T170000
DTSTAMP:20260924T125148Z
UID:20260929T230000Z-24052@calendar.santarosa.edu__20261103
ATTACH:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/live/image/gid/3/width/80/height/80/
 crop/1/src_region/0,0,322,322/730_sistah_2_sistah.rev.1790278878.png
CATEGORIES:Department Events
DESCRIPTION:Sistah 2 Sistah is a welcoming space for Black girls and young
  women to connect\, uplift\, and empower one another.  Through sisterhood\
 , conversation\, wellness\, education\, leadership\, and creative experien
 ces\, students can build meaningful relationships while growing personally
  and academically.  Topics and activities may include:Sisterhood &amp\; co
 mmunity  Self-love and confidence  Academic &amp\; career success  Wellnes
 s and life skills  Leadership and personal growth  Cultural identity and s
 elf-discovery  For more information\, visit the Sawubona BLOC website. (ht
 tps://bloc.santarosa.edu/august-2026)  The Sawubona BLOC is located in Pio
 neer Hall\, Room 360 (next to the bookstore) on the Santa Rosa Campus.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260924T200612Z
LOCATION:Pioneer Hall\, Room 360 - Santa Rosa Campus
URL:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/event/24052-sistah-2-sistah
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Sistah 2 Sistah is a welcoming space for
  Black girls and young women to connect\, uplift\, and empower one another
 .</p><p>  Through sisterhood\, conversation\, wellness\, education\, leade
 rship\, and creative experiences\, students can build meaningful relations
 hips while growing personally and academically.</p><p>  Topics and activit
 ies may include:</p><ul><li>Sisterhood &amp\; community  </li><li>Self-lov
 e and confidence  </li><li>Academic &amp\; career success  </li><li>Wellne
 ss and life skills  </li><li>Leadership and personal growth  </li><li>Cult
 ural identity and self-discovery  </li></ul><p><a href="https://bloc.santa
 rosa.edu/august-2026" target="_blank" rel="noopener">For more information\
 , visit the Sawubona BLOC website.</a></p><p>  The Sawubona BLOC is locate
 d in Pioneer Hall\, Room 360 (next to the bookstore) on the Santa Rosa Cam
 pus.</p>
